<+># GestureRecognition\nCreating a neural network to work in tandem with a walking quad-legged robot do. This hand recognition will be used to give commands to the quad-legged bot.\n\n## Install packages \nEither activeate the .venv file\n\n`python -m ~/HandRecognition/.venv/bin/activate`\n\nor \n\ninstall the correct packages\n\n`pip install -r ~/HandRecognition/requirements.txt`\n\n\n## Resources I used to create this project\nTutorial Playlist:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5gdOLiKZgus&list=PLJfV3mV9d1ZWOX3YAjFI0ItJ9q2I0ARUY&index=7\n\nOverview on MediaPipe and how it works. \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=a99p_fAr6e4&list=PL0FM467k5KSyt5o3ro2fyQGt-6zRkHXRv\n\n## Some tools I expect to use for this project include:\n1. MediaPipe \n    https://developers.google.com/edge/mediapipe/solutions/guide#get_started\n2. hand-gesture-recognition-ENG\n    https://github.com/kinivi/hand-gesture-recognition-mediapipe\n3. OpenCV\n    https://docs.opencv.org/5.0/main_modules/api_root.html\n    \n# Libraries planned on using:\n## OpenCV \n\nUsed to capture frames from camera source and then processing the frames.\n\n## MediaPipe\n\nThis is the engine that pre-processes the captured frames to then process hand-tracking, detection of finger orientation events.\n\n## PyAutoGUI\nUsed to control mouse cursor and perform clicks based off of hand gestures.\n\n## PyNput\nUsed for mouse and keyboard events. \n\n## NumPy\nUsed for numerical operations, distance calculations. Majority would be used for array handling.\n\n## Time\nUsed to track time during execution\n\n## Math\nUsing to calculate disance between angles on hand orientations and gestures\n\n
